After having ascended V, M, T and C I decided to do Healer. I had
always had trouble with them and this time was no exception. My first
three attempts failed miserably but then I decided to change _one_
thing and hey, my next character made it.

The mistake I made was that I didn't wear any body amour at the start
because I wanted to use those healing spells. Of course my AC was
really high because of that and the monsters did much more damage -> I
had to use my spells _a lot_. It was a vicious circle. After putting an
elven mithril coat on I was much more safe than with those spells.

With my improved AC I made it to the mine town. The altar was
co-aligned so I did some sacrifising and got Magicbane. It was exactly
what I wanted since I was going to go genoless and the thought of
facing Ls without it sent shivers down my spine. *brrr* I also found a
magic lamp there and got a wish. I wished for Grayswandir. Later I
kinda regretted spending a wish on that piece of junk because it just
wasn't that effective on a Healer although it was blessed and +7...
Guess my good memories of having that on a Tourist interfered with my
judgment or something.

I did some polypiling in the gnomish town with a wand of polymorph
because I wanted the spellbook of identify. Didn't get it. Got some
other books and tried to read them. Which was VERY risky but I needed
to learn the lesson... Read one a couple of times in the temple but it
was too difficult - got paralysed and blind and so on but no wrenching
sensations. Guess I just wouldn't take no for an answer and still tried
to read it. This time felt a wrenching sensation and got paralysed and
four ants almost ate me. When I had a chance to act I had only ONE hit
point left out of the 80 or so I had had. Quick thinking, what would
jesus do etc, and I decided to use my wand of digging to escape. Didn't
know if there were any charges left but luckily there was. Phew! Sorry,
Team Ant, better luck next time. :P

After that I played with more care 'cause this character had it really
going on and I didn't want to experience YASD. Sokoban gave me BoH
which was useless 'cause I had already required one from a bones file
of a Wizard (who had died of touching a cockatrice corpse). I was
pretty nervous about not having reflection - I didn't want to die YAAD
either. But then a nice silver dragon left her scales and I could ditch
the mithril coat - and finally use those nice little spells! :)

I got one throne geno but didn't want to use it. Didn't get anything
useful from the thrones besides that (if that can be called useful when
going genoless...) so I guess I could have kicked all the 5 thrones to
pieces - hmm, gold pieces...

Cyclops was a loser. Hit him with a sleep spell then whacked him with
Grayswandir. Felt like a total coward for not letting him defend
himself but that feeling soon passed when I got my hands on the Staff
of Aesculapius. It was the first time I had it and I liked it. It was
particularly fun to whack annoying trolls with it and see them losing
their levels and then never rising again. Hee hee. Suits them.

After quest I did Fort Ludios, Medusa, Castle. Nothing interesting
happened. Some liches annoyed me, that's all. Castle wand of wishing
was (0:1), wished for charging, b+ofID, helm of brilliance, gauntlets
of dexterity and a magic marker. Got some protection from priests and
enchanted armour, AC was -39.

Gehennom. I was kinda surprised to meet Asmodeus on the upstairs of his
lair, then I remembered my poor archeologist who died there because she
didn't have her gloves on when picking up a cockatrice corpse (well,
that was a model example of a YASD, because she had a 1:3 wand of
wishing and a magic lamp but she thought she was so good that she don't
need any amulets of life saving or any stupid trinkets like that.
Should have known better. :/).  Asmodeus zapped a wand of digging and
cowardly escaped, I went after him and ended somewhere else than him.
Oh well, decided to leave him be where-ever he was hiding.

The archeologist's bones was a gold mine. Used some time sorting all
that stuff out. Decided to take the Orb of Detection with me 'cause
there was a helm of opposite alignment too. I did of course lose all my
protection, AC went to -30 and the Orb was heavy as hell. I was
burdened from that on (except in the planes).

Killed Juiblex (who didn't even engulf me), killed Vlad, killed
Yeenoghu (summoned by some random &) and killed Orcus. Found the VS (DL
52, why'd it have to be so down?), then went to meet Yendor. Zapped a
wand of death, took the book and headed down. Seems like that was when
the problems started.

A MMF got to my brain. Missed him three times with a wand of death.
Lost some information. I had to wish for a new spellbook of magic
mapping instead of writing one 'cause the MMF prefered that information
particularly much (the other spells he didn't want to take from me). I
also foolishly used two wishes for ROBES when I was at DL 50 (didn't
remember  that there was a source for robes a couple of levels lower...
Sometimes I just don't think what I'm doing. :D)

Sanctum was easy. Took the amulet and started my long climb up. And I
can tell you it was _long_! I kept on going back and forth the same
levels. I nearly had a nervous breakdown because of the stupid
mysterious force and the stupid liches and stupid trapdoors that were
under some stuff and the stupid Yendor appearing once in a while and
stupid nasties surrounding me and stupid master mind flayers sucking my
brains out and all that crap and I had to do Jublex's swamp five times
(and there was a master lich and an arch lich pleasuring me with their
tricks) and there was Asmodeus and there was Baalzebub, more liches and
a gremlin had stolen my ability to teleport (still had the teleport
control) so I had to use my wands and scrolls of teleport in order to
beat those Ls in the race towards the upstairs. But then I finally
arrived in the VotD and what a relief it was! I guess it was one of the
happiest NH moments for me.

Yendor appeared some times after that but soon I was at my chest at DL
1 and did some final preparations. Earth: easy, used GD. Air: easy too,
found portal by accident. Fire: bit more of a challenge, didn't want to
use GD (should have), five Archons started summoning, had to start
conflicting in order to move, but then I saw the portal and moved there
as fast as I could (I didn't want to lose yet another character to the
Plane of Fire, that's just really really sad). Water: used 3 GDs, third
time the portal was right next to me but it was under a boulder and I
was levitating so couldn't push it. Fortunately I knew the spell of
force bolt, so bye bye boulder, you're not going to the astral but I
am...

Astral: Didn't use conflict. Usually I enjoy killing everything that
moves there and collecting their stuff but now I just wanted to get it
over with. First altar, Famine, lawful. Second altar, Death, chaotic.
Third, mine. To get there I had both Pestilence and Famine next to me,
I was ill. Zapped wand of death at P, applied a uni horn and gave F a
taste of Grayswandir (well, guess it wasn't THAT crappy after all) and
then teleported everything out of my way and sacrificed the Amulet.

Goodbye GisMyAss! the Demigoddess...

